In this case, OLD(_items.Count) accesses the value of the '_items' list before it is modified, and _items.Count accesses the modified value after it has been added.

This only checks if the count of elements in '_items' has increased or not, without actually verifying whether the capacity increases by 'x'. The actual increase of capacity usually depends on the internal implementation details of the ArrayList class, and it may not directly correspond to the actual number of elements added to the list. Hence, this doesn't directly answer the question in terms of verifying the increase of the array list's capacity as part of its size.--------------------
